## 6. FINDING STRUCTURE

Every finding must have:

```json
{
  "id": "CRITICAL-001",
  "severity": "CRITICAL",
  "category": "Null Safety",
  "file": "src/main/resources/dw/mappings/account-mapping.dwl",
  "line": 101,
  "issue": "Array access without null check - accessing [0] on filter result",
  "impact": "NullPointerException when filter returns empty array",
  "pass": 1
}
```

### Severity Classification

| Severity | Criteria | Impact |
|----------|----------|--------|
| **CRITICAL** | Runtime crash, data loss, security hole | Production blocker |
| **HIGH** | Logic error, configuration issue, type mismatch | Major issue |
| **MEDIUM** | Code quality, hardcoded values, low coverage | Quality issue |
| **LOW** | Naming, style, minor improvements | Minor issue |

### ID Naming Convention

- CRITICAL-001, CRITICAL-002, ... (sequential across ALL passes)
- HIGH-001, HIGH-002, ...
- MEDIUM-001, MEDIUM-002, ...
- MAPPING-001, MAPPING-002, ... (for field mapping issues)

**IDs are sequential across passes.** If Pass 1 ends at CRITICAL-002, Pass 2 starts at CRITICAL-003.

