## 8. QUALITY SCORING

### Score Calculation Method

```
START: 100 points

DEDUCTIONS:
- Per CRITICAL bug: -6 points (Implementation Quality)
- Per HIGH bug: -2 points (Implementation Quality)
- Per MEDIUM bug: -1 point (Code Quality)
- Missing requirements doc: -10 points (Requirements Compliance)
- Low test coverage (<50%): -10 points (Code Quality)
- Missing error handlers: -5 points (Architecture)
- Hardcoded values: -2 points each (Code Quality)

CATEGORY CAPS:
- If 7+ critical bugs: Implementation Quality = 0
- If no requirements: Requirements Compliance max = 15
- If <30% test coverage: Code Quality max = 10
```

### Category Breakdown

| Category | Max | How to Score |
|----------|-----|--------------|
| **Requirements Compliance** | 25 | Requirements met? (15 if no doc provided) |
| **Implementation Quality** | 25 | Critical/High bugs found? (0 if 7+ critical) |
| **Architecture & Design** | 20 | Patterns, error handling, separation |
| **Code Quality & Tests** | 20 | Test coverage, clean code, no hardcoding |
| **Security & Compliance** | 10 | Credentials externalized, PII protected |

### Grade Thresholds

| Score | Grade | Production Ready |
|-------|-------|------------------|
| 90-100 | EXCEPTIONAL | ✅ Yes |
| 80-89 | EXCELLENT | ✅ Yes |
| 70-79 | GOOD | ⚠️ Conditional |
| 60-69 | ACCEPTABLE | ❌ No |
| 0-59 | POOR | ❌ No |

