## 13. RGV MULTI-PASS ANALYSIS STRATEGY

### Why Multi-Pass Works

LLMs miss ~15-30% of issues in single pass due to:
- **Attention drift** on long files (early content gets less scrutiny)
- **Context window saturation** (too many files dilute focus)
- **Pattern fixation** (finding one bug, missing adjacent ones in same file)
- **Error handler path blindness** (focus on happy path, skip error paths)
- **Cross-file interaction blindness** (miss how flows connect)

### Per-Pass Guidelines

| Rule | Why |
|------|-----|
| Full sweep of ALL files every pass | Don't assume prior pass was complete |
| Don't re-read previous findings before starting | Avoid anchoring/confirmation bias |
| Approach each pass as if first time | Fresh perspective catches more |
| Focus on what COULD go wrong | Not what you already found |
| Tag every finding with pass number | Delta tracking is mandatory |

### Delta Detection Rules

| Rule | Definition |
|------|------------|
| A finding is "new" | Not already reported in prior passes |
| Compare by | file + line + issue category (not exact wording) |
| Same file/line, DIFFERENT issue | Count as NEW |
| Same issue, DIFFERENT line | Count as NEW |
| Duplicate of prior pass | Do NOT count (skip it) |

### Convergence Definition

```
converged = (new_critical_count == 0) AND (new_medium_count == 0)

Note: new HIGH findings alone do NOT block convergence.
Rationale: HIGH findings are important but don't indicate
the review is still discovering fundamental issues.
```

### RGV Few-Shot Example

❌ BAD — Skipping passes because "found enough":
```
Pass 1 found 8 bugs. That seems thorough enough, proceeding to Phase 4.
```

✅ GOOD — Always run default passes:
```
Pass 1: 8 findings (2C, 3H, 3M)
Pass 2: 3 new findings (1C, 0H, 2M) — not converged
Pass 3: 1 new finding (0C, 1H, 0M) — CONVERGED (0 new Critical/Medium)
Total: 12 findings across 3 passes
```

❌ BAD — Anchoring on prior findings:
```
Pass 2: Re-checking the 8 bugs from Pass 1... all confirmed.
No new bugs found. Converged.
```

✅ GOOD — Fresh perspective:
```
Pass 2: Full sweep of all flows with fresh eyes.
Found CRITICAL-003 in process-order-flow.xml:52 —
scatter-gather timeout propagates null to downstream transform.
This was missed in Pass 1 due to focus on individual route errors.
```

