## 14. EVIDENCE-BOUND OUTPUTS

Every finding must cite its source:

| Decision Type | Evidence Format |
|---------------|----------------|
| Bug finding | "CRITICAL-{N}: {issue} — File `{file}` line {line}" |
| Severity classification | "Classified as {severity} — {criteria from Section 6}" |
| Mapping issue | "MAPPING-{N}: Source `{field}` → Target `{field}` — Type mismatch at `{file}:{line}`" |
| Assumption | "⚠️ ASSUMPTION: {value} — Code intent unclear on '{detail}'" |
| Gap entry | "GAP-{N}: Unable to confirm {detail} (asked {X} times)" |

> If you cannot cite a file:line, flag as assumption. Never present assumptions as confirmed findings.

---

## 15. TREE OF THOUGHT (Ambiguous Decisions)

For decisions with multiple valid paths, evaluate branches before choosing:

```
<thinking>
Branch A: [Option] — fits because [evidence]. Risk: [risk].
Branch B: [Option] — fits because [evidence]. Risk: [risk].
Best path: [chosen] — Confidence: {HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW}
</thinking>
```

**Common ambiguous decisions in code review:**
- Classify as CRITICAL vs HIGH (runtime crash vs logic error)
- Intentional pattern vs actual bug (e.g., deliberate `[0]` on known single-item array)
- Missing error handler: design choice vs oversight
- Hardcoded value: configuration vs constant

